    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "The Observer pattern defines a one-to-many dependency. When one object changes state, all dependents are notified automatically."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "language": "javascript",
        "caption": "Observer in JavaScript",
        "code": "class EventEmitter {\n  on(event, listener) { this.events[event].push(listener); }\n  emit(event, data) { this.events[event].forEach(l => l(data)); }\n}\n\nconst emitter = new EventEmitter();\nemitter.on(\"update\", data => console.log(data));\nemitter.emit(\"update\", { id: 1 });"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "key-terms",
      "data": {
        "terms": [
